  <div class="prose">
    <h2>The work</h2>
    <p>"Our installations and constructions are made mostly of recycled materials, love and devotion!" wrote the collective. The figures, for their part, are those of the Facebook page: three years of work in June 2013; "36 months and more than 4,000 hours of work" in May 2013, and some 14,000 hours of work in all, by Christian's count; four years of existence on June 9, 2014, "what evolution, what lessons and what work during these crazy years". The clearing of the bunker, the lodges, the walkways, the stages, the treehouses, the tipi, the electricity and the network deep into the forest: all of it was done by hand, by four to six people depending on the season, and by the friends who came "to drop by".</p>
    <blockquote><p>"It may seem impossible to the intellectuals, but it only takes four motivated people and two days of work. An excellent challenge and a lesson in living in nature."</p><cite>Call to build a permanent stage in the trees, September 2012</cite></blockquote>
  </div>
